 the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","Better was 42…Qa2+ (−1.49), which moves the attacked queen to safety."],"better":"42…Qa2+ saves the attacked queen. After 43.Rf2 Qc4 44.Qxc4+ Rxc4 45.Rb3 Rb8, the queens come off (−1.49)."},{"ply":85,"name":"43.Qb3+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"43.Qb3+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The queen forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","The queen joins the attack: it now hits 2 squares around the Black king.","The next best move, 43.Rb3, would drop White's winning chances from 50% to 35% (−1.73).","43.Qb3+ forks the king and the pawn.","Moves the attacked queen to safety.","Black answers 43…Rf7."]},{"ply":87,"name":"44.Rfe1","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"44.Rfe1! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The rook takes the open e-file, aiming at the rook on e4 behind the rook on e3.","Doubles rooks on the e-file, so the two pieces push in the same direction.","The next best move, 44.Rxe4, would drop White's winning chances from 50% to 29% (−2.41).","44.Rfe1 stops …Rxe3 and takes the open e-file, aiming at the rook on e4 behind the rook on e3.","Black was threatening …Rxe3, winning a rook. Rfe1 takes care of it.","Black answers 44…f5, pushing the pawn storm towards the king."]},{"ply":98,"name":"49…Nc5","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"49…Nc5 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 51% to 31%.","points":["White answers 50.Nxf8, which takes the rook on f8.","After Nxf8, White wins 2 points of material within 3 moves.","Better was 49…Rb8 (−0.16), which moves the attacked rook to safety."],"better":"49…Rb8 gets the rook out of the way of Nxf8. After 50.Ne5 Nc5 51.Nc4 Ne4 52.Rb5 Rc8 53.Nxb6 Rc3, Black is a pawn down (−0.16)."},{"ply":113,"name":"57.Rf3+","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"57.Rf3+ is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 73% to 5%.","points":["Black answers 57…Nxf3, which takes the rook on f3.","After Nxf3, Black wins 5 points of material within 2 moves.","Better was 57.Rb3 (+2.76): the rook takes the half-open b-file, aiming at the b6 pawn."],"better":"57.Rb3 takes the half-open b-file, aiming at the b6 pawn, and attacks the b6 pawn, which is undefended. After 57…Kf7 58.Kg3 Kg8 59.Rxb6 Ne4+ 60.Kf4, White comes out a pawn up (+2.76)."}],"opening":{"name":"Italian Game: Classical Variation, Giuoco Pianissimo","eco":"C54","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 7.O-O: 13 moves in all, 7 by White and 6 by Black.","Theory runs out after 7.O-O: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}